       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). The 1,700 mg single dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- Another dose you have in mind\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me that and I'll enter it as written with a note that you confirmed the dose."
